# Camera movement
@scenario tutorial_lesson_13
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[char ginger global on]
[set ui.dialogueFadeMs 160]
[stage clear]
[show ginger guide thoughtful]
ginger: Stay where you are. I'll bring the camera closer so you can see my expression.
[if !tutorial_still]
timeline {
  parallel {
    move "ginger" { x:-48 y:24 dur:640 easing:ease_out }
    scale "ginger" { sx:1.16 sy:1.16 dur:640 easing:ease_out }
  }
}
[endif]
ginger: Compare the two keyframes in Puppeteer. Watch my face as the shot gets tighter.
> Review question -> check
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
ginger: Why pair a small pan with a zoom?
> To adjust the subject’s framing as it grows. -> correct
> To change the speaker name. -> retry
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
[show ginger guide confused]
ginger: Position and scale together control where the subject lands in the frame. Give it another try.
[jump check]
@label correct
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: Position and scale together control where the subject lands in the frame.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
@label return_hub
[if !tutorial_done_13]
[flag tutorial_done_13]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_2]
